CAT = "s63BrokerDealers"; SEG = "BDR"
Q = [
("Under the Uniform Securities Act, which person is NOT a broker-dealer?",
 "An issuer selling its own stock", ["A firm trading for customers", "A dealer buying for inventory", "A firm selling for others for fees"],
 "The USA excludes agents, issuers and banks, savings institutions and trust companies from the broker-dealer definition. Firms that effect trades for others or for their own account are broker-dealers."),
("Which of these is excluded from the USA definition of broker-dealer?",
 "A savings institution", ["An online trading firm", "A municipal bond dealer", "A firm selling private placements"],
 "Banks, savings institutions and trust companies are excluded from the broker-dealer definition. Dealing only in exempt municipal bonds or private placements does not take a firm out of it."),
("Under the USA, an individual who sells securities on behalf of a registered firm is:",
 "An agent, not a broker-dealer", ["Both an agent and a broker-dealer", "A broker-dealer only", "An issuer"],
 "The USA excludes agents from the broker-dealer definition. The individual registers as an agent, and the firm she represents registers as the broker-dealer."),
("A broker-dealer with no office in State M sells only to insurance companies and banks there. In State M it is:",
 "Not a broker-dealer there", ["Required to register there", "Required to notice file there", "Required to register its agents only"],
 "A firm with no place of business in the state that deals only with issuers, other broker-dealers and institutional buyers such as banks and insurance companies is outside the state's broker-dealer definition."),
("A broker-dealer with no office in State R begins soliciting individual residents of State R. Under the USA it:",
 "Must register in State R", ["Is excluded as an out-of-state firm", "Needs only a notice filing", "Must register only its agents"],
 "The exclusion for out-of-state firms covers only business with issuers, other broker-dealers and institutions. Soliciting individual residents requires registration in that state."),
("FINRA Rule 3110 requires each member firm to establish and maintain:",
 "Written supervisory procedures", ["A customer insurance fund", "A state-approved fee schedule", "An on-site SEC examiner"],
 "Rule 3110 requires a supervisory system and written procedures reasonably designed to achieve compliance with securities laws and FINRA rules. SIPC, not the firm, provides customer protection on failure."),
("A broker-dealer applying to register with the SEC and the states through the CRD system files:",
 "Form BD", ["Form U4", "Form ADV", "Form U5"],
 "Form BD is the uniform application for broker-dealer registration. Form U4 registers individuals, Form U5 ends their registration, and Form ADV is for investment advisers."),
("Under NSMIA, a state's net capital requirement for a registered broker-dealer:",
 "Cannot exceed the SEC's", ["Must be twice the SEC's", "Is set by FINRA alone", "Applies only to new firms"],
 "NSMIA bars states from imposing capital, custody, margin, financial responsibility, recordkeeping, bonding or reporting requirements on broker-dealers that differ from or add to federal rules."),
("Under FINRA Rule 3110, a branch office that does not supervise other offices must be inspected at least:",
 "Every three years", ["Every single year", "Every five years", "Every six months"],
 "OSJs and supervisory branch offices are inspected at least yearly. Non-supervisory branches are inspected at least every three years, and non-branch locations on a regular periodic schedule."),
("FINRA Rule 3110 requires an annual compliance meeting with:",
 "Each registered representative", ["Each customer with a margin account", "The state Administrator", "Only branch managers"],
 "Each registered representative must attend an interview or meeting at least once a year at which compliance matters relevant to their activities are discussed."),
("Under FINRA Rule 3110, a firm must designate:",
 "A principal for each type of business", ["A state examiner for each office", "An agent to approve every trade", "A customer advocate per branch"],
 "The supervisory system must designate an appropriately registered principal with authority to carry out supervisory responsibilities for each type of business the firm engages in."),
("Under FINRA Rule 3110, the person who inspects a branch office generally may NOT be:",
 "The branch's own manager", ["The firm's chief compliance officer", "An internal auditor", "A regional principal"],
 "To keep inspections independent, the branch manager or anyone reporting to that manager generally may not conduct the inspection of that branch, with narrow exceptions for very small firms."),
("An agent churns accounts for months while the branch manager ignores exception reports. The Administrator may act against:",
 "The firm and the agent", ["Only the agent", "Only the customer's bank", "No one, if losses are repaid"],
 "Failure to reasonably supervise agents is a ground under USA Section 204 to deny, suspend or revoke a broker-dealer's registration. The agent is also liable for the churning itself."),
("A firm with an office in the state sells only municipal bonds to retail customers there. Under the USA it:",
 "Must register as a broker-dealer", ["Is excluded because munis are exempt", "Needs only a notice filing", "Must register the bonds"],
 "Exempt securities need no registration, but the persons who sell them still must register. A firm with a place of business in the state that effects trades for customers is a broker-dealer."),
("Which may a state Administrator still require of a registered broker-dealer under NSMIA?",
 "Registration and filing fees", ["Higher net capital than the SEC", "Extra margin rules", "Longer record retention"],
 "States keep the power to register firms, charge fees, require filings of documents filed with the SEC and enforce antifraud rules, but may not add to federal financial and recordkeeping rules."),
("Under the USA, which of these is NOT a 'person'?",
 "A deceased individual", ["A trust", "A government", "An unincorporated association"],
 "The USA defines a person to include individuals, corporations, partnerships, associations, trusts, unincorporated organizations and governments. A deceased individual can no longer act as a person."),
("A firm buys bonds for its own inventory and resells them to customers at a markup. It is acting as:",
 "A dealer (principal)", ["A broker (agent)", "An investment adviser", "An issuer"],
 "A firm acting for its own account is a dealer and earns a markup. Acting for a customer's account, it is a broker and earns a commission."),
("If information on a broker-dealer's Form BD becomes inaccurate, the firm must file an amendment:",
 "Promptly", ["Within 90 days", "At year-end renewal", "Only if asked"],
 "Form BD must be amended promptly when its information becomes inaccurate, so regulators and the CRD system always hold current information about the firm."),
("Under Section 15 of the Securities Exchange Act, a broker-dealer using the mails or interstate commerce to sell securities generally must:",
 "Register with the SEC", ["Register only in its home state", "Join a stock exchange", "File with the Federal Reserve"],
 "Section 15(a) makes it unlawful for a broker or dealer to use interstate commerce to effect securities transactions unless registered with the SEC, apart from narrow exceptions."),
("A dealer has one office in State X, sells only to State X residents and uses no exchange. Under Section 15 of the Exchange Act it may:",
 "Skip SEC registration", ["Skip state registration", "Skip both registrations", "Sell only exempt securities"],
 "Section 15(a) exempts a broker-dealer whose business is exclusively intrastate and makes no use of an exchange. It still must register with its state."),
("FINRA Rule 3110 lets a firm review an agent's outgoing correspondence:",
 "Using a risk-based approach", ["Only after a complaint", "Only once a year", "By the agent's self-certifying"],
 "Rule 3110 allows risk-based review of correspondence, by keyword or other means, under written procedures. Reviews must be documented, and agents may not review their own correspondence."),
("Under FINRA Rule 3110, every registered person must be assigned to:",
 "A registered supervisor", ["A FINRA examiner", "A state Administrator", "A customer service desk"],
 "The supervisory system assigns each registered person to an appropriately registered representative or principal responsible for supervising that person's activities."),
("A broker-dealer's agent meets customers and takes orders from her home office. Under the USA that home office is:",
 "A place of business", ["Not subject to regulation", "A branch only if it has staff", "Exempt as a residence"],
 "A place of business is any location from which a firm's securities business is conducted or held out as conducted, including a residence used to meet customers and take orders."),
("A firm has an office in the state but deals only with banks and insurance companies there. Under the USA it:",
 "Still must register there", ["Is excluded from the definition", "Needs only a notice filing", "May register its agents only"],
 "The institutional-only exclusion applies only to firms with no place of business in the state. A firm with an office there is a broker-dealer in that state, whoever its customers are."),
]
